SUMMARY:[minor] Princeton - Solicitation policy for religious and non-comme
 rcial groups (RRR 3.2.2)
LOCATION:Princeton University
DESCRIPTION:SCALE: minor\n\nDirectly governs faith-based outreach: 'As a ge
 neral rule\, representatives of noncommercial off-campus organizations\, s
 uch as political\, religious\, and charitable groups\, will not be permitt
 ed to solicit on campus.' Exceptions apply to ODUS during business hours\,
  are limited to 9am-5pm\, one or two people per location and five or six o
 n campus total\, and normally six visits per month. Preferred sites includ
 e adjacent to Chancellor Green\, the north side of Frist\, and near the Un
 iversity Store east entrance.\n\nOUTREACH NOTE: Sponsorship by a member of
  the University community is explicitly preferred. Policy confirmed unchan
 ged as of 2026-08-10.\n\nSOURCE: https://rrr.princeton.edu/university-and-
 community/32-regulations-governing-solicitation-distribution-and-peaceful-
 dissent\n\n(Compiled 2026-08-10. Verify before acting.)
CATEGORIES:Princeton\,minor
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
